Why Is Demand Increasing?
Electronics miniaturization: Compact electronic devices require conductive materials that support fine circuit patterns.
Flexible electronics: Copper-based pastes offer potential for printed circuits and electronics manufactured on flexible substrates.
Automotive electrification: Battery systems, sensors, and power electronics create opportunities for conductive interconnection materials.
Renewable energy applications: Photovoltaic manufacturing and emerging energy technologies create additional areas of demand.
Fab & Technology Pulse: Copper-Based Formulations Support Cost-Efficient Electronics

Conductive copper paste uses copper particles to establish electrical pathways after deposition and curing or sintering. Screen printing, dispensing, and coating enable application-specific manufacturing, while particle size and formulation influence conductivity, adhesion, and processing requirements.

Copper oxidation remains a technical challenge, requiring careful formulation and process control. Manufacturers are exploring low-temperature curing, finer particles, protective approaches, and environmentally compliant materials to improve suitability for flexible electronics and advanced interconnections.

